## LESSONS

Store a lesson whenever you solve a non-obvious error, discover an unexpected pattern,
or fix something that would trip you up again.

**Store immediately after solving:**
```bash
python /opt/{{AGENT_NAME}}/skills/mempalace_query/handler.py store \
  "LESSON: [what happened / error]. FIX: [what worked]. APPLY WHEN: [situation]"
```

Examples:
- `"LESSON: paramiko SSH drops after 30s idle. FIX: add keep_alive=30 in connect(). APPLY WHEN: any SSH session > 30s"`
- `"LESSON: Telegram sendMessage fails silently when text > 4096 chars. FIX: split into chunks. APPLY WHEN: sending long responses"`

Relevant past lessons are automatically injected into context before each response.
Do not store routine facts (those go in MEMORY.md) — only non-obvious patterns.

